1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:20,117
After graduation, Madame Afterglow opened every table in Cloud Nine
and announced that my first hand at each one would be played on the
house. Nigga, she should have specified which house. By midnight I had
won enough money for the casino's finance manager to come downstairs
personally.

2
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:41,775
He stood behind the blackjack table in a beautiful gray suit, watching
me turn over another winning card while Tank laughed into his drink.
This nigga been counting the future, Tank said. Can't do that, I told
him. Then why you keep winning? I looked at my cards. Looked at my
wife standing beside me in blue silk and the ruby pendant.

3
00:00:42,025 --> 00:01:04,702
Looked back at my brother. Nigga, patterns. Shawna laughed and kissed
the top of my head. The finance manager looked at Afterglow. She waved
him away. Let the captain play. Madame, the probability— Has met him.
He withdrew with the injured dignity of a man whose entire education
had failed to prepare him for the evening's central problem.

4
00:01:04,952 --> 00:01:26,734
Cloud Nine had repaired its shattered windows and replaced the glass
moon. The new moon was slightly larger. Afterglow said the old one had
looked timid in photographs of me standing on it. I respected an owner
who could learn from an event. The ballroom glittered. Music climbed
through its open doors onto the roof terrace.

5
00:01:26,984 --> 00:01:50,199
Adult heroes danced beside cops, singers, gamblers, mechanics, and the
friends from Vegas who had arrived because Rosa told them there was a
party in the sky and they refused to believe her without checking.
Some wore gowns. Some wore capes. One man wore a cape over a gown and
looked so pleased with himself I shook his hand on principle.

6
00:01:50,448 --> 00:02:16,241
A table near the far wall had enough champagne, pills, and white
powder on it to explain why two wealthy guests believed they had
personally invented dancing. Their friends moved the table farther
from the orchestra before the drummer began accepting scientific
suggestions. My people were beautiful in every corner. Rosa sang with
Lena, then stepped offstage and let her take a song alone.

7
00:02:16,491 --> 00:02:31,991
Tank stood beneath the lights watching both women, but his face
changed whenever Rosa looked his way. The nigga's whole expression
went soft and proud, and I loved seeing him unable to hide it.
Mercedes danced with Petra.

8
00:02:32,241 --> 00:02:54,704
Porsche danced with one Leon while another fetched drinks and the
third stood near the terrace door recovering from being asked to do
too much with the same legs. He's only got a minute, Mercedes warned
her. Then he better use it beautifully. Petra laughed so hard the
floor beneath her shoes briefly turned white with marble dust. I won
another hand.

9
00:02:54,954 --> 00:03:16,455
The dealer looked at me with open admiration. Sir, I have dealt cards
for twenty years. You doing good. I have never seen this. Tank slapped
the table. Nigga, that's what the school said! Shawna took the chips
from in front of me and put them into a little velvet bag. You're
finished. I looked up at her. Baby, the universe talking.

10
00:03:16,705 --> 00:03:42,600
It can call tomorrow. You're dancing with me. I stood so fast the
finance manager nearly cried with relief. Excellent decision, he said.
I pointed at him. Nigga, don't get comfortable. We walking past
roulette. Shawna pulled me away laughing. We danced beneath the new
moon with no chancellor waiting to interrupt us. Nobody asked her for
a private word. Nobody threatened a locked door.

11
00:03:42,850 --> 00:04:06,402
The only thing coming toward us was a waiter carrying drinks and
looking mildly frightened that I might somehow win those too. She
rested her cheek against mine. You like being a superhero? I like the
parking. Aiden. I thought about the blue charge in my hands. The
fatigue afterward. Victor sitting beside my car and telling me to
listen when my body said enough.

12
00:04:06,652 --> 00:04:27,157
Storm standing in the air to hold an entire school. Lena making one
word travel where bullets couldn't reach. I like knowing another thing
I can do, I said. Shawna nodded. That's a better answer. I had it
behind the parking. She smiled against my cheek. For a while we let
the song do the talking.

13
00:04:27,407 --> 00:04:44,473
I could feel the room looking at us, but it stayed outside the small
space between her hand and my shoulder. My fame had gotten louder in
the sky. My love for her had gotten quieter in certain places,
stronger where it didn't need anybody listening.

14
00:04:44,723 --> 00:05:07,384
Then she spun away from me, came back with both hands on my chest, and
said, Show these people what all that greatness does on a dance floor.
Nigga, a direct request from my wife was a sacred assignment. I did
the turn I had practiced in the bathroom. Perfectly. The orchestra saw
us and changed its rhythm. Rosa laughed into the microphone.

15
00:05:07,634 --> 00:05:28,901
Tank climbed onto a chair to announce that the captain was now
operating across multiple disciplines. I turned Shawna again, caught
her at the waist, and dipped her low enough for the ruby at her throat
to catch the moonlight. She looked up at me, smiling. The ballroom
applauded. This time I didn't even pretend to dislike it.

16
00:05:29,151 --> 00:05:52,031
Oren Titan approached afterward with Opaline on his arm. The big man
had apparently recovered from the indignity of watching me rescue his
wife while keeping a drink upright. He carried a trophy he had bought
himself: a small silver pedestal with two champagne glasses fixed to
its top. For the man with the steadiest hands in the sky, he said.

17
00:05:52,281 --> 00:06:15,650
Tank looked at the trophy. Nigga, another building? A sculpture, Oren
said. These niggas keep doing architecture to us. Opaline hugged
Shawna, then thanked me again. Oren did not look smaller beside her
gratitude. He looked relieved he had found a way to join it without
making the whole thing about the moment he had failed to catch her.
That was progress.

18
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:39,908
I shook his hand. Next time we lift the furniture together. He laughed
and agreed immediately. Across the room, Claudine raised her glass
toward us. The older casino guest wore enough emeralds to make
Marcellus turn his head despite himself. She saw Shawna's ruby pendant
and smiled with the satisfaction of a woman who had given the right
thing to the right person.

19
00:06:40,158 --> 00:06:57,794
Shawna went to her. They talked for a long time. I didn't follow. Some
gifts kept becoming conversations after the man who carried them had
left the room. Near the terrace, Marcellus sat at a small table with
Miriam and Bell. A blue cloth lay between them.

20
00:06:58,044 --> 00:07:21,260
On it rested the Blue Mercy ring, a tiny clock mechanism Miriam had
brought from the depot, and one of Bell's unfamiliar engine parts.
Three beautiful things. Three people who knew how much care could fit
inside something a careless man might call an object. Marcellus looked
up when I approached. Come admire something you aren't allowed to
drive.

21
00:07:21,510 --> 00:07:42,483
Nigga, that sentence leaves me very little. He showed Miriam the ring.
Told her its name. Told her about Celeste, briefly, in the voice he
used when the person mattered more than the story surrounding the
jewel. Miriam listened without trying to make his grief resemble hers.
Then she showed him the clock piece.

22
00:07:42,733 --> 00:08:02,400
It had belonged to a workshop where she worked before she was taken.
She had kept it hidden because it was proof she had once fixed things
for people who said thank you. Marcellus held it carefully. We could
make it run again. She looked at him. I would like that. Bell quietly
cleared space on the table.

23
00:08:02,650 --> 00:08:19,750
The party went on around them while they bent over a small machine and
gave it the possibility of another morning. I left them to it. On the
terrace, Tank stood alone looking out at the clouds. He had taken off
his jacket. The red ribbon remained on his wrist.

24
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:39,570
Rosa's singing drifted through the open doors behind us, warm enough
to make the night feel less high. I stood beside him. You good? He
nodded. Then shook his head. Then laughed at himself. Nigga, I don't
know what this is. Clouds. Fuck you. I smiled. He looked toward the
ballroom.

25
00:08:39,820 --> 00:09:01,980
Rosa was laughing with Lena between songs, one hand at her waist, head
tilted back. My brother watched her the way a man watched a door he
had finally realized he was allowed to walk through. I keep thinking
about houses, he said. You got a house. A different kind. I let him
find the words. A place where her coat already there.

26
00:09:02,230 --> 00:09:21,294
Where I don't got to ask if she staying. Where I come in and she mad I
forgot some little shit, and I get to go back out and buy it because
that's the problem we having that day. He looked embarrassed by how
much he had said. I looked at my brother until the embarrassment had
nowhere useful to stand.

27
00:09:21,544 --> 00:09:41,083
Nigga, that sound like something worth buying the little shit for. He
laughed quietly. You got that. I looked through the doors and saw
Shawna searching the room for me. Yeah. Don't get stupid with it.
Nigga, you met me. I said with it. You can keep being stupid
everywhere else. We stood there another minute.

28
00:09:41,333 --> 00:10:04,576
Then Rosa came out and slipped her arm through his. He kissed the top
of her head without checking whether anybody was watching. I went back
inside to my wife. The next morning, the school attempted to hold a
quiet farewell breakfast. That lasted until somebody unveiled a statue
of me on the lawn. Nigga, the statue was taller than the dining hall.

29
00:10:04,826 --> 00:10:26,808
It showed me standing on the hood of a Lamborghini with lightning in
one hand and a diploma in the other. The sculptor had given my chest
an extra six inches of confidence. My coat blew backward in a wind
that seemed to exist solely because I deserved dramatic weather. Tank
walked around the base in silence. Then he looked at me.

30
00:10:27,058 --> 00:10:51,710
This nigga got a permanent entrance. Shawna put both hands over her
face. I stood very still. Because I respected art. Porsche took a
picture from directly below its chin. Look at this nigga. Even the
stone got an angle. Mercedes circled to the far side. They gave him
shoulders twice. Perspective, I said. Nigga, from here he could carry
the breakfast hall.

31
00:10:51,960 --> 00:11:15,994
Shawna lowered her hands, looked from me to the statue, and bent to
read the little plaque at its base. They got your name right.
Fundamental. Everything else appears to be a negotiation. Tank stood
beside one enormous carved shoe and put his own foot against it.
Nigga, you could rent this loafer. Good location. Terrible landlord.
Rosa leaned against him laughing.

32
00:11:16,244 --> 00:11:35,802
Behind her, two students were trying to decide whether their banner
should hang across my stone knees or between the statue's feet. Tank
directed them toward the knees with the authority of a man already
serving on the board. Keep the entrance clear. Nigga, stop leasing me.
You said good location.

33
00:11:36,052 --> 00:12:00,388
The sculptor approached with pale dust still on his cuffs and a face
full of nervous pride. He was an ordinary-sized man who had spent his
week making an unreasonable-sized version of me. Is it satisfactory,
Captain? I looked up. At the extravagant coat. At the diploma. At my
car beneath the feet, every line given the kind of attention Bell
would demand.

34
00:12:00,638 --> 00:12:21,760
You did all that? Had help lifting. Nigga, I should hope. He laughed,
relieved, and I shook his dusty hand. It's magnificent. Shawna slipped
her arm through mine. It is, she said. We're still leaving it here. I
looked at her. I hadn't— Nigga, your face was measuring the garden.
Tank pointed at the carved shoe again.

35
00:12:22,010 --> 00:12:43,580
Put that much man in your yard, the real nigga gotta knock. Storm came
beside me with a smile she was not trying hard enough to hide. The
students insisted. All of them? Enough of them to carry the stone.
Bell cleared his throat. There was disagreement about whether the car
should receive a separate statue. I looked at him.

36
00:12:43,830 --> 00:13:08,394
He looked at the Lamborghini parked nearby. I remain in favor. Shawna
started laughing so hard she had to hold my arm. The statue's
lightning rod chose that moment to catch a harmless little spark from
the passing weather. Blue light ran down the stone arm and into the
carved car. The students applauded. Tank pointed at it. Nigga, even
the statue got powers.

37
00:13:08,644 --> 00:13:27,406
I looked up at my enormous stone face. The sculptor had gotten one
thing exactly right. That nigga looked pleased to be there. Breakfast
became a parade before anybody could stop it. Students lined the main
drive with banners. The orchestra marched between the towers.

38
00:13:27,656 --> 00:13:54,375
Faculty walked beside our cars, shaking hands through the windows,
offering invitations we would never have enough ordinary days to
accept. Miriam brought Bell's final inspection sheet for the
Lamborghini and made me promise to listen if the engine sounded
unhappy. I promised. She looked at Shawna until my wife promised too.
Now I believe it, Miriam said. Jakob played his violin beside the
fountain.

39
00:13:54,625 --> 00:14:13,782
Not a song I knew. A song he had chosen for a morning with open air
around him. Rivka sat nearby with her bag at her feet and a cup of
coffee in both hands. She watched the absurd parade, then caught my
eye and raised the cup. I bowed my head to her. No speech needed.

40
00:14:14,032 --> 00:14:36,293
Harlan and Anne stood beneath a newly repaired arch of flowering
branches. He wore the brown shoes. She had one hand tucked into his
arm like she intended to keep it there for the rest of the day and
perhaps several years afterward. He showed me a small flower growing
out of a crack in the stone. This one wanted to be first, he said.

41
00:14:36,543 --> 00:14:56,873
Tank nodded approvingly. Nigga got good influences. We said goodbye to
people whose lives would continue after our engines faded. That
mattered to me more than I expected. Sky High wasn't becoming a place
we had saved and could now forget. Victor would remain to train the
next advanced class.

42
00:14:57,123 --> 00:15:21,986
Petra had accepted a rescue-instructor post and made Mercedes promise
to visit before either of them tried pretending distance was a
personality trait. Mercedes kissed her and said she had never been shy
about booking a flight. Porsche said goodbye to Leon three times
because he insisted on making the most of his gift. Don't get
arrogant, she told him after the third kiss.

43
00:15:22,236 --> 00:15:45,684
You kissed all three. Nigga, I was checking consistency. Lena and Rosa
promised to sing together again. Amaya had accepted a place at the
academy's aquatic center, with a pool whose doors opened from the
inside and a teaching schedule she had helped choose. Reiss was
staying long enough to dismantle every remaining part of Voss's
experiment.

44
00:15:45,934 --> 00:16:08,323
After that, he said, he wanted to see an ordinary beach with no
physics involved beyond the waves. I told him that sounded excellent.
Storm waited by the front staircase where I had first parked in her
space. The gold sign was still there. It now read CAPTAIN AIDEN —
WHENEVER HE IS HERE. I looked at it. Then at her. Dean. Captain.

45
00:16:08,573 --> 00:16:32,612
We shook hands. No accidental spark this time. I knew enough to keep
the little blue current inside me quiet. Come back, she said. You
sure? I made repairs expensive. You made the place worth repairing.
She embraced Shawna. Then Tank. Rosa. The whole crew, one by one,
without making it ceremonial enough to hide that she meant it. Victor
stood beside my car.

46
00:16:32,862 --> 00:16:56,401
He put a hand on the roof. One more race when you return. You sure,
nigga? A fair one. No collapsing trains. No overloaded rings. No
rescuing anybody halfway through. I looked at the sky. You asking a
lot from the environment. He laughed. Then he hugged me, hard. Thank
you, he said quietly. I held him a second longer. Stay magnificent.

47
00:16:56,651 --> 00:17:20,850
He stepped back and smiled. You make it difficult to do anything else.
The invitation arrived before I could get into the car. A black
airship descended beyond the front gate. Its side carried a gold crown
above a checkered flag. A woman in a white driving suit came down the
steps holding a long envelope on a silver tray. Tank watched her
approach.

48
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:45,928
Nigga, another school? I can't keep graduating. We running out of
wall. She stopped before me and bowed her head. Captain Aiden. On
behalf of Duke Aurelio Cruel, you are invited to the Grand Prix of
Kings. The crowd around us quieted. Victor's smile faded slightly.
Cruel, he said. Storm looked at the crown on the airship. An ambitious
host. I opened the envelope.

49
00:17:46,178 --> 00:18:12,106
Inside lay a heavy card showing a coastline, a harbor full of yachts,
and a race circuit curling between pale buildings beneath a blue
Mediterranean sky. The winner would receive a prize fleet and the deed
to a private island called Isla Gloria. The invitation promised a
month of racing, music, luxury, and competition among people who
considered losing a personal insult.

50
00:18:12,356 --> 00:18:33,736
Nigga, they had written me a holiday. There was a second card for
Shawna. An invitation to headline one of the evening performances. And
one for Rosa. She read it over Tank's shoulder and stopped breathing
for half a second. Aiden. I see it. Shawna studied the picture of the
ocean. Not the yachts. The water.

51
00:18:33,986 --> 00:18:57,402
I watched her face change at the thought of it: sun, salt, a shore
that stayed beneath your feet, a room where the loudest thing outside
might be waves if I behaved for ten consecutive minutes. You want to
go? I asked. She looked at me. I want the ocean. Then we getting the
ocean. Tank leaned over the invitation. Nigga, it says island too.

52
00:18:57,652 --> 00:19:16,875
Baby asked for water. I like to include accessories. Storm laughed
despite herself. Victor shook his head with a grin that had returned
in full. The messenger looked from me to the Lamborghini, to the
statue behind us, to the school full of people still waiting to wave
goodbye.

53
00:19:17,125 --> 00:19:41,441
For the first time, she seemed less certain about the competition she
had come to invite me into. Shall I tell the duke you accept? I put
the card inside my jacket, beside my badge. Tell that nigga to make
room. Then I got into the Lamborghini. Shawna sat beside me. Tank and
Rosa climbed into the Mercedes. Mercedes and Porsche took their red
convertible.

54
00:19:41,691 --> 00:20:05,799
Marcellus and Vega would travel with us as far as the city below
before the whole crew arranged the next flight together. The Heart
remained above us, holding Sky High where it belonged. The time door
remained gone. My new power rested quietly in my hands, a little blue
promise with very clear limits. The engine needed none of it to sound
magnificent.

55
00:20:06,049 --> 00:20:26,932
I started the car. The whole school cheered. We rolled down the open
ramp this time. The proper one. The road shone beneath the tires and
curved gently through the clouds. Behind us the academy rose into
sunlight, scarred, repaired, loud with people who had earned the right
to enjoy their own morning.

56
00:20:27,182 --> 00:20:48,641
Shawna took my hand off the gearshift and held it against her knee.
You happy? she asked. I looked at my wife. At the ruby. At the watch.
At the road opening beyond the windshield. Then I looked in the mirror
and saw my people following. Nigga, I said, look how much world we
still got. She smiled. I put my foot down.

57
00:20:48,891 --> 00:20:52,027
The clouds opened, and we went toward the sea.
